## Implemented integration

- `EditorOverlayFrameSnapshot` is CPU-owned, immutable, and bound to frame serial, document revision, selection revision, mapping epoch, viewport generation, projection revision, and view revision.
- `DesktopGizmoIntegrationAdapter` owns the desktop Gizmo priority domain and falls back to the P6 router for unconsumed events. Primitive selection resolves to its owning node; the scene root never enters the node Gizmo route.
- Camera input runs before adapter snapshot construction. Camera navigation and picking are suppressed only during an active adapter drag. Modal/ImGui-captured hover moves do not consume input.
- Snap is conditional on `snapEnabled`; translation uses grid-unit snap. Drag previews use immutable drag-start TRS. Node, selection, and mapping fence changes detach stale drags fail-closed. Stable Gizmo IDs mix the complete 64-bit document authority.
- Production order is `FinalColor -> EditorHighlight -> EditorOverlay -> Present -> ImGui`; the legacy ImGui overlay producer is disabled.
- Overlay preparation is slot-ready and queue-token bound. Prepare, resolve, abandon, resize, and shutdown reconcile tickets without device idle; shutdown runs before pass graph destruction while the RHI device is alive.
- CMake wires CPU Gizmo/Grid, RHI overlay, desktop input, focused tests, shader generation, and Android exclusion. Android shader isolation covers both `.slang` and `.glsl`.
- Vulkan sparse logical argument slots use one lazily-created empty descriptor-set layout in `rhi/vulkan/VulkanDevice.h/.cpp`. This fixed the real `VUID-VkPipelineLayoutCreateInfo-graphicsPipelineLibrary-06753` found by the first smoke.
- A second real finding, `VUID-vkCmdDraw-None-09600`, showed read-only ImGui views registered as `readWrite`. `render/SceneResources.cpp:539-548` now registers them as `sampledRead`, matching their ShaderRead layout.

